WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A handler can return successfully and still save two receipts. Test the resulting state.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Call your real workflow code. Replace its external service with a model you write.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Here the model saves the receipt, then loses the acknowledgement. The handler retries.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Use ctx.at to schedule the payment and a duplicate webhook.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Use ctx.expect to check the exact receipt. You define what correct means.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Run your adapter with the workflow-sim CLI. Each run starts in a fresh worker process.

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.000
The virtual clock drives the real retry at two seconds and redelivery at five.

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The result contains your failed check, expected content and actual content.

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Expected one exact receipt. Found two. A successful handler was not enough.

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Fix the key in your handler. Keep the same modeled failure and assertions.

11
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Run again. One exact receipt; all four checks match. PASS for this modeled run.

12
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
You supply the workflow, service models and assertions. workflow-sim controls execution and reports the evidence. Private alpha: github.com/KarthikRaju391.
